From 594ab08d176f2662a25959177ef8abf2d3606747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:59:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: never map a T-CONT onto a channel another
 one owns

gpon_tcont_entity_to_index() falls back to channel (entity - 0x8000) + 1
when the entity is not in the map, as long as that channel has an
Alloc-ID. That matches a first provisioning, where the T-CONTs take the
channels in entity order. After a GPON restart they are rebuilt in the
order the services come back, and each takes the first free channel.

On the Archer XR500v, after pulling the fibre, 0x8001 (Alloc-ID 513)
and 0x8002 (769) came back first and took channels 1 and 2. For 0x8000
(257) the fallback then returned channel 1 because it had an Alloc-ID,
so 0x8000 was never rebuilt: Alloc-ID 257 was not programmed, and the
internet GEM port went up on Alloc-ID 513's grants. Downstream was fine
but a speed test gave 27 Mbit/s instead of 700.

Only fall back to a channel no other entity owns, so 0x8000 goes
through the rebuild path and gets a channel of its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 5607a2854..eb691391c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -950,8 +950,16 @@ static int gpon_tcont_entity_to_index(struct xpon_priv *priv, u16 entity_id,
 	    entity_id < 0x8000 + GPON_MAX_TCONT - 1) {
 		unsigned int fallback = (entity_id - 0x8000) + 1;
 
+		/*
+		 * The fallback only holds while channels follow the entity
+		 * order, as on a first provisioning.  After a restart the
+		 * T-CONTs are rebuilt in whatever order the services come
+		 * back, so never hand out a channel another entity owns.
+		 */
 		if (fallback < GPON_MAX_TCONT &&
-		    priv->tcont_alloc_id[fallback] != GPON_TCONT_UNASSIGNED)
+		    priv->tcont_alloc_id[fallback] != GPON_TCONT_UNASSIGNED &&
+		    priv->tcont_entity_id[fallback] ==
+		    GPON_TCONT_ENTITY_UNASSIGNED)
 			found = fallback;
 	}
 	if (found >= 0)
